// NOT THE SITE. This branch exists only to deploy the redirect Worker that keeps the first
// workers.dev address, `aurigen`, answering after the site moved to theplatbook.com.
//
// Why a branch: deploying a second Worker needs a Cloudflare key, which this machine does not
// have, and adding an automation file for it needs a GitHub permission this machine does not
// have either. The existing "Aurigen site" workflow takes the branch to deploy as an input and
// deploys whatever `cloudflare/wrangler.jsonc` on that branch names, so this branch names the
// redirect instead of the site.
//
// To deploy it: GitHub, Actions, "Aurigen site", Run workflow, mode restore, restore_branch
// forward/aurigen-redirect, tick the confirm box. The run's LAST step fails on purpose: it
// checks the old address for a page (200) and gets a redirect (301). The deploy itself happens
// in the step before, and the log ends with "Uploaded aurigen". Ignore the red cross.
//
// WHEN MERGING main INTO THIS BRANCH, KEEP THIS FILE. Taking main's version would hand
// theplatbook.com and the site's assets to the `aurigen` Worker, which would take the live site
// down. This file must stay: no routes, no assets, no database, no cron. (No cron also matters
// on its own: the free plan allows 5 cron triggers per account and the site needs one.)
{
  "$schema": "node_modules/wrangler/config-schema.json",
  "name": "aurigen",
  "main": "src/forward.js",
  "compatibility_date": "2026-10-01",
  "workers_dev": true,
  "triggers": { "crons": [] },
  "observability": { "enabled": false }
}
